A table renamed twice, two releases apart (`menu`, then `carte`, then
`meal`), deployed at once to a database still at `menu`: the steps run in
order, each on what the one before left. No chain to follow back.

== before
CREATE TABLE menu (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO menu VALUES (1, 'lunch');

== after
CREATE TABLE meal (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== ledger
ALTER TABLE menu RENAME TO carte;
ALTER TABLE carte RENAME TO meal;

== plan
roux: migrating test.db, ledger.sql's steps 1 to 2
  step 1
    ALTER TABLE menu RENAME TO carte;
  step 2
    ALTER TABLE carte RENAME TO meal;
roux: migrating test.db, 4 steps
  table `meal`: aside, to make it anew
    ALTER TABLE "meal" RENAME TO "roux_old_meal"
  table `meal`: as schema.sql makes it
    CREATE TABLE meal (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT
  table `meal`: its rows, by id, title
    INSERT INTO "meal" ("id", "title") SELECT "id", "title" FROM "roux_old_meal"
  table `meal`: the old one
    DROP TABLE "roux_old_meal"

== query
SELECT id, title FROM meal

== rows
1 | lunch
